s. That is how errors propagate.\n\nThe **one exception** is the nine `vector-index` files (covering all 1,805 vectors). I will provide the exact **schema** for those files, but the actual population of each vector with verified archival citations, NARA box/folder numbers, LOC manuscript references, and cryptographic hashes is a **harvesting task** that belongs to Agent Omega. That is what it was built for.\n\nEverything else — every skill, every dataset registry, every workflow, every template, every rule — gets written now. No empty files. No gaps.\n\n---\n\n## MISSING FILE 1: `.antigravity/skills/archival-retrieval.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nskill:\n  id: \"archival-retrieval\"\n  name: \"Archival Retrieval & Primary Source Acquisition\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n\n  capabilities:\n    - \"Query NARA catalog API by Record Group, Entry, Box, and Folder\"\n    - \"Query Library of Congress Manuscript Division by Collection, Box, and File\"\n    - \"Query CIA CREST reading room by document ID and keyword\"\n    - \"Query GPO govinfo by Congressional session and document type\"\n    - \"Query foreign national archives: AGI (Spain), TNA (UK), ANOM (France), AN (Cuba)\"\n    - \"Query SlaveVoyages.org by voyage ID, port, and date range\"\n    - \"Query OpenCorporates and ICIJ by entity name, jurisdiction, and officer\"\n    - \"Retrieve PACER docket sheets by case number and court\"\n    - \"Retrieve FCSC certified claim ledgers from NARA RG 234\"\n    - \"Retrieve Presidential Library materials by administration and collection\"\n\n  retrieval_protocols:\n    citation_completeness:\n      nara: \"Record Group / Entry / Box / Folder / Document Title / Date\"\n      loc: \"Collection Name / Box / File / Document Title / Date\"\n      cia: \"CREST Document ID / CIA-RDP Number / Title / Date / Classification\"\n      foreign: \"Archive Name / Fondo / Legajo / Expediente / Folio / Date\"\n    verification:\n      - \"Every retrieved document must be cross-referenced against at least one independent source\"\n      - \"If a document is referenced in the 1,805-vector index but cannot be located, flag as PENDING_VERIFICATION\"\n      - \"If a document contradicts the vector index, flag for Red Team review\"\n    output_format:\n      - \"PDF or TIFF image of original document\"\n      - \"SHA-256 hash of downloaded file\"\n      - \"Timestamped retrieval log entry\"\n      - \"Full citation string in Bluebook 21st Edition format\"\n\n  quality_gates:\n    - \"No document enters the evidentiary record without a SHA-256 hash\"\n    - \"No document enters the evidentiary record without a complete citation\"\n    - \"No document enters the evidentiary record without provenance logging\"\n    - \"All retrievals logged to 00_Master_Knowledge_Base/Retrieval_Log.md\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## MISSING FILE 2: `.antigravity/skills/red-team-stress-test.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nskill:\n  id: \"red-team-stress-test\"\n  name: \"Adversarial Stress-Testing & Vulnerability Audit\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n\n  capabilities:\n    - \"Simulate DOJ Civil Division Rule 12(b)(1) sovereign immunity motions\"\n    - \"Simulate DOJ Rule 12(b)(6) failure-to-state-a-claim motions\"\n    - \"Simulate Rule 56 summary judgment opposition briefs\"\n    - \"Simulate political question doctrine dismissals (Baker v. Carr analysis)\"\n    - \"Simulate act-of-state doctrine defenses (Banco Nacional v. Sabbatino)\"\n    - \"Simulate statute of limitations strikes (28 U.S.C. § 2501)\"\n    - \"Simulate national security and state secrets privilege assertions (United States v. Reynolds)\"\n    - \"Simulate Daubert challenges to expert witness testimony\"\n    - \"Simulate retroactive legislative ambush and jurisdiction-stripping riders\"\n    - \"Simulate tri-branch collusion scenarios (executive-legislative-judicial coordination)\"\n    - \"Simulate Rule 23 class certification opposition (numerosity, typicality, adequacy attacks)\"\n    - \"Simulate FSIA immunity defenses for corporate instrumentalitie